To find the definite integral of \(f(x)=x^{2}\) from \(x=1\) to \(x=3\):

\[
\int_{1}^{3} x^{2}\,dx=\left[\frac{x^{3}}{3}\right]_{1}^{3}
   = \frac{(3)^3}{3}-\frac{(1)^3}{3}
   = \frac{27}{3}-\frac{1}{3}
   = \frac{26}{3}.
\]

So,

\[
\boxed{\displaystyle \int_{1}^{3} x^{2}\,dx = \frac{26}{3}}
\]

which equals approximately **\(8.\overline{66}\)**.
